  "term": "gonadotropin-releasing hormone",
  "definition": "Gonadotropin-releasing hormone is a peptide made by neurons in the hypothalamus that is released into blood leading to the pituitary gland. It stimulates the pituitary to produce and release luteinizing hormone and follicle-stimulating hormone.",
